Usages:
  subclass_pattern: |
    `Exchange` is the base class; roughly 25 concrete per-exchange classes (one file each, e.g.
    `Binance`, Kraken, Bybit, Okx) override only the behaviors where that exchange's ccxt
    implementation diverges from the common case (fee schedules, order types, leverage-tier
    fetching, websocket quirks). MAP_EXCHANGE_CHILDCLASS maps exchange id strings to these
    subclasses for ExchangeResolver to pick the right one.

Annotations: |
  This cell owns all outbound communication with a cryptocurrency exchange (via ccxt/ccxt.pro):
  market data, order placement, balances, and fees. It is a near-leaf in the spine — it depends
  on nothing else documented here, so every other cell that needs market data or trading
  primitives imports from this cell, never the reverse.

  Use `subclass_pattern` when deciding whether new exchange-specific logic belongs in `Exchange`
  (if universal) or in a per-exchange subclass (if it isn't).

---

"Exchange(config: dict[str, Any], exchange_config: dict[str, Any] | None, validate: bool, load_leverage_tiers: bool)":
  location: exchange.py
  annotations: |
    Wraps one ccxt/ccxt.pro exchange connection (sync + async clients) plus freqtrade-specific
    behavior overrides and, when the exchange supports it, an `ExchangeWS` websocket session.

    `config`: full runtime configuration; `exchange_config` overrides just the exchange section
    `validate`: run market/pair/timeframe/order-type validation during construction
    `load_leverage_tiers`: pre-fetch leverage tier data for margin/futures trading
  properties:
    "name -> str": |
      Human-readable exchange name.
    "id -> str": |
      ccxt exchange id (matches MAP_EXCHANGE_CHILDCLASS keys).
    "timeframes -> list[str]": |
      Timeframes this exchange's API supports.
    "markets -> dict[str, Any]": |
      All markets/pairs known to the exchange, keyed by pair symbol, as returned by ccxt.
    "precisionMode -> int": |
      ccxt amount/price precision rounding mode for this exchange.
    "precision_mode_price -> int": |
      Precision rounding mode specifically for price values (may differ from precisionMode).
  methods:
    "get_historic_ohlcv(pair: str, timeframe: str, since_ms: int, candle_type: str, is_new_pair: bool, until_ms: int | None) -> candles:DataFrame": |
      Fetch historical OHLCV candles for `pair` from `since_ms` (paginating as needed).

      `candle_type`: spot/futures/mark/funding-rate candle series to fetch
      `candles`: OHLCV rows as a DataFrame
    "refresh_latest_ohlcv(pair_list: list[tuple[str, str, str]], since_ms: int | None, cache: bool, drop_incomplete: bool | None) -> data:dict[str, Any]": |
      Bulk-refresh the most recent OHLCV candles for every (pair, timeframe, candle_type) in
      `pair_list`, using the websocket session when available.

      `cache`: reuse previously fetched candles instead of re-requesting the full history
      `data`: refreshed candles keyed by (pair, timeframe)
    "klines(pair_interval: tuple[str, str], copy: bool) -> candles:DataFrame": |
      Return the cached OHLCV DataFrame for one (pair, timeframe) tuple.

      `copy`: return a defensive copy rather than the cached DataFrame itself
    "fetch_ticker(pair: str) -> ticker:dict[str, Any]": |
      Fetch the current ticker (last price, bid/ask, volume) for `pair`.
    "get_tickers(cached: bool, market_type: str | None) -> tickers:dict[str, Any]": |
      Fetch tickers for all (or one market type's) pairs in a single call where supported.
    "get_rate(pair: str, refresh: bool, side: str, is_short: bool, order_book: dict[str, Any] | None, ticker: dict[str, Any] | None) -> rate:float": |
      Compute the entry/exit price to use for `pair`, applying the configured pricing method
      (ticker-based or order-book-based).

      `side`: "entry" or "exit"
      `rate`: price to use for the next order
    "create_order(pair: str, ordertype: str, side: str, amount: float, rate: float, leverage: float, time_in_force: str, reduceOnly: bool, initial_order: bool) -> order:dict[str, Any]": |
      Place a real order on the exchange (or simulate one in dry-run mode).

      `order`: raw ccxt-shaped order response
    "cancel_order(order_id: str, pair: str, params: dict[str, Any] | None) -> order:dict[str, Any]": |
      Cancel an open order by id.
    "fetch_order(order_id: str, pair: str, params: dict[str, Any] | None) -> order:dict[str, Any]": |
      Fetch the current state of a previously placed order.
    "get_balances(params: dict[str, Any] | None) -> balances:dict[str, Any]": |
      Fetch account balances from the exchange.
    "get_fee(symbol: str, order_type: str, side: str, amount: float, price: float, taker_or_maker: str) -> fee:float": |
      Compute the trading fee rate applicable to a hypothetical order.
    "reload_markets(force: bool, load_leverage_tiers: bool)": |
      Re-fetch and cache the exchange's market list, refreshing markets.
    "validate_config(config: dict[str, Any])": |
      Validate that `config`'s exchange section, pairs, timeframe, and order types are all
      supported by this exchange; raises ConfigurationError/OperationalException otherwise.

"Exchange::Binance()":
  location: binance.py
  annotations: |
    Binance-specific overrides of `Exchange` (futures funding-fee handling, order-type
    restrictions, leverage-tier fetching). One of roughly 25 such per-exchange subclasses; see
    `subclass_pattern`.

"ExchangeWS(config: dict[str, Any], ccxt_object: Any)":
  location: exchange_ws.py
  annotations: |
    Background websocket session (its own thread + asyncio loop) that keeps OHLCV candles for
    subscribed (pair, timeframe) pairs warm via ccxt.pro, so Exchange.refresh_latest_ohlcv
    can serve them without a REST round-trip.
  methods:
    "schedule_ohlcv(pair: str, timeframe: str, candle_type: str)": |
      Ensure a background watch loop is running for this (pair, timeframe, candle_type).
    "get_ohlcv(pair: str, timeframe: str, candle_type: str, candle_ts: int) -> response:OHLCVResponse": |
      Await the latest websocket-delivered candles for one (pair, timeframe), up to `candle_ts`.
    "cleanup()": |
      Stop the background thread and close the websocket connections.
    "reset_connections(cleanup: bool)": |
      Tear down and, unless `cleanup` is True, immediately re-establish websocket connections.

"timeframe_to_minutes(timeframe: str) -> minutes:int":
  location: exchange_utils_timeframe.py
  annotations: |
    Convert a timeframe string (e.g. "5m", "1h", "1d") to its length in minutes.

"timeframe_to_seconds(timeframe: str) -> seconds:int":
  location: exchange_utils_timeframe.py
  annotations: |
    Convert a timeframe string to its length in seconds.

"market_is_active(market: dict[str, Any]) -> active:bool":
  location: exchange_utils.py
  annotations: |
    True if a ccxt market dict represents a pair that is currently tradeable (not delisted,
    not expired).

"validate_exchange(exchange: str) -> result:tuple[bool, str, str, Any]":
  location: exchange_utils.py
  annotations: |
    Check whether `exchange` is a ccxt-known id and whether freqtrade has verified it.

    `result`: (is_valid, reason, exchange_id, ccxt_class_or_none)

